Constructors-
        -a constructor is special block that has same name as class and runs
            automatically when we create an object using new keyword.
        -it has no return type
        -same name as class name
        - called automatically when object is created
      -Types
          1.Default Constructor
                -constructor without parameter.
                -if you don't create any, java automatically create one.
          2.Parameterized constructor
                -it accept parameters to set the values.
          3.copy constructor
                -java does not provide build_in copy constructors like c++.
                -we create it manually.
                -if we change the value from copy constructor it doesn't change value
                    of copied constructor.
syntax-
     1.Default constructor

            className(){
              //body of constructor
            }
     2.parameterized constructor

            className(int name,...(parameters...)){
                // body of constructor
            }
     3.Copy constructor

            className(constructor_name instance_name){
            this.variable-name = instance_name;

            }